## detect_silence : Finds the quiet stretches of the timeline and REPORTS them, changing nothing — the read half of Clip ▸ Remove Silences…, whose Remove button sends the answer to ripple_delete_ranges. In voice mode (the default) a moment is quiet when the cached Silero VAD probability over it is under voice_confidence; a clip whose source window holds no voice anywhere, and every file when the model cannot be used, is judged by level — each 10 ms of the cached waveform times the audio envelope against threshold_db. In either mode a moment whose envelope alone puts full scale at or under threshold_db is quiet, so volume, fades, ducking, mute and another track's solo all count. A run quieter than threshold_db and at least min_length long is a candidate; it then loses padding at each end, and its bounds snap INWARD to the frame grid — which can leave a frame of room tone, where outward would clip the attack of the next word. A moment no clip in scope covers is not a candidate at all: a hole in the timeline is not dead air. The result reports the scope and mode it used, and names any media whose analysis is still running rather than counting it silent — the waveform, or in voice mode the speech. judged_by_level_clips names each clip judged by level, and proposed_by_mix_clips each clip a range is proposed inside only because the mix turns it down while its analysis is still running. A nest clip is a wall: no candidate reaches into one, and protected_nests names each nest clip a quiet run of at least min_length crossed — set_scope into it and call again to look for any dead air inside.
